not repeat it.","No proving command or fixture is described for the unhappy fetch path."],"finding":"AC3/AC4 mandate the lock 'FAILS CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched' but no acceptance criterion supplies a way to prove the fail-closed path actually fails closed — there is no test/check that simulates a fetch failure and asserts the build errors.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fede5e967c04b7963","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (superseding list), bullets 3 and 4","norm_id":"n77a32ee79685d630","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Implementer writes a lock that fails closed on parse mismatch but still silently continues (or the fetch error path is untested), and CI is green because the happy-path ACs all pass."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State a proving command that forces the fetch to fail (e.g. point the base ref at a nonexistent branch or empty the fetched file) and assert the gate step returns a non-zero exit code.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"medium","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The AC 'The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched' has no described proving mechanism. Simulating a git-fetch-of-main failure in CI is non-trivial, and the plan names no test, fixture, or command that exercises the fetch-failure branch. Without one, the fail-closed behavior is asserted but unverified — the same class of latent bug the plan is fixing in the module-size lock.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1ec2757ef272436d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched'","norm_id":"n1685779e58a7bfa7","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Factor the base-value fetch into a script whose failure path is unit-testable, and add a test that runs it with an unreachable ref and asserts a non-zero exit.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"medium","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the semantic lock's behavior when the baseline file is ABSENT on `main` (bootstrap = allow), and ensure that case is distinguished from a failed/flaky fetch (which must fail CLOSED) — mirroring the module-size lock's `git cat-file -e` bootstrap branch.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Module-size lock distinguishes the two cases: `_build-and-test.yml:377-378` — \"`git cat-file -e` distinguishes 'main has the limit file -> compare' from 'main lacks it -> bootstrap (allow)'\"","The plan's semantic table enumerates removed/lowered/raised/added but not 'baseline absent on base'","AC3: 'The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base copy cannot be fetched — no ::warning::-and-continue' — does not carve out the legitimate absent-on-main case"],"finding":"The semantic lock's mechanism does not specify behavior when `.github/complexity-baseline.json` is ABSENT on `main` (the change that first introduces the file, or history predating the gate). The module-size lock it is modeled on explicitly handles this via `git cat-file -e` (main lacks it -> bootstrap/allow), but AC3's 'FAIL CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched' collides with this: a naive fail-closed treats 'no baseline on main' identically to 'fetch flaked', which would permanently reject the file-introducing change and block every change whenever main lacks the file.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f512393bddcef8594","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"CORRECTION section 'Resolution: the lock is SEMANTIC' and AC3 (supersedes list)","norm_id":"n6b309190784925ad","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["The commit that first adds .github/complexity-baseline.json (base has no such file to parse)","A branch based on history predating the gate is rebased/verified while main already has the file"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a table row / AC: 'baseline absent on the fetched base -> ALLOWED (bootstrap), detected via `git cat-file -e <base>:.github/complexity-baseline.json`', kept distinct from 'fetch failed -> FAIL CLOSED'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["verify command `grep 'complexity-baseline' .github/workflows/` inspects output with `grep` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P9"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["file_impact is empty"],"finding":"No file_impact declared on a leaf work ticket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b56a0701da43def","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n6324407e6516f811","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Record the {path, reason} files this work will touch (e.g. via set_file_impact) so the attestation is scoped to them.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify a bounded retry/backoff (or a clearly-distinct 'infrastructure error' vs 'lock violation' exit path) for the base fetch so a transient flake retries before the lock fails closed, rather than blocking the build on the first hiccup.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T6","T9"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a failed git fetch of main emits a warning and then runs the cap ... so a change raising 800 to 5000 passes on any run where that fetch flakes'","The plan's own framing establishes that fetches DO flake; failing closed on the first flake with no retry converts every flake into a blocked build.","No retry/backoff/timeout policy for the base fetch is mentioned."],"finding":"The plan flips the module-size lock and the new complexity lock from fail-open to fail-closed on a `git fetch` of main, but never addresses that transient fetch flakes will now HARD-FAIL builds; no retry/backoff on the fetch is specified, so the design trades an insecure fail-open for a brittle fail-closed with a new false-failure surface.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9170f4ab8ca764e1","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"CORRECTION section and superseding AC3/AC4","norm_id":"n74d5004e885885d0","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A transient GitHub network hiccup during `git fetch origin main` now blocks an unrelated PR's CI until it is re-run or an administrator overrides."],"severity":"none","suggested_f